**CHAPTER 3 – TRAINING MANAGEMENT ****AND ASSESSMENT ****DETAILS**

## TRAINING STRATEGY

- The training requirement will be achieved through rationalized training delivery (RTD) and two CAF-delivered components consisting of:

- Mod 1 – RTD, based on POs 001 – 005: This module will entail post secondary education delivered by an accredited Canadian institution recognized through the CAF-ACE as being aligned with CYBER OP training and education requirements;

- XXXXXX – Foundational Knowledge and Skills Assessment (FKSA)

- Mod 2, 3, and 4 – Residential, based on PO 006 - 010: These modules entail training related to defending the DND/CAF cyber domain that cannot be provided by an external educational institution.

## TRAINING DURATION

- Training and education for POs 001–005 will be delivered by various educational institutions vetted via CAF-ACE. Acceptable programs vary in length from two to four semesters (i.e., 1 – 2 academic years), and each educational institution structures their programs differently. As such, no EOs have been developed for POs 001–005 given the difficulty involved in developing a training plan flexible enough to account for all program designs. Additionally, there is currently a lack of subject matter experts within the CAF to develop the content. In light of these issues, MPG HQ determined that the POs in Chapter 2 (i.e., POs 001–005) were sufficiently detailed to provide the foundation needed to complete the CYBER OP CAF-ACE entry (i.e., a detailed training plan is not required at this time given the depth of the PO standards).

- Training for POs 001 to 005 will require a maximum of 450 calendar days in accordance with contract W4938-20069S/001/ZH, however, this is subject to change as the training matures. Training for POs 006 to 010 will require a maximum of 61.42 instructional training days (ITDs) based on instructional and testing time only (See Annex D – Timetable).

- training days are based on 7 x 50 min periods/day;

- training days have been adjusted to exclude physical training, administration, worship, course photos, graduation, course reports, kit issue and return and briefings;

- the MPGTG 1.2 multiplier converts 61.42 ITDs to 73.7 resourced training days (RTDs). For resource calculations, 73.7 is rounded up to 74 RTDs and is then multiplied by a factor of 7/5 (= 1.4) and results for a total of 103.6 weekend resourced training days (WRTDs) or “calendar days” which rounds up to 104 WTD; and

- this training will comprise the following training times:

- 61.42 (61) ITDs;

- 73.68 (74) RTDs; and

- 103.6 (104) WRTDs or calendar days.

