- applicable network traffic;

- applicable network connections; and

- applicable network defence tools.

- denied:

- artificial intelligence;

- assistance;

- unapproved tools/equipment; and

- unapproved scripts.

- environment: computer labs with access to CSTE(Z) or unclassified internet.

- Standard: IAW specified references, the student shall triage IDS alerts by:

- generating IDS alerts;

- categorizing IDS alerts;

- investigating network traffic related to alert data; and

- determining validity of alerts.

- Time Required:

- EO - 13 x 50 min periods;

- EC 007.01 - 007.03 - 2 x 60 min period; and

- EC Review - 1 x 50 min period.

- Instructional Methods:

- interactive lecture;

- guided discussions;

- demonstration; and

- practical exercises/labs.

- Training Aids:

- display connected to instructor workstation;

- whiteboard, with markers and eraser;

- PowerPoint slides containing key information related to lessons (e.g., definitions, diagrams, etc.);

- simulated enterprise network;

- malicious network traffic;

- packet analysis software; and

- various scripting engines.

