- Remarks: Nil

- Teaching Points:

| Lesson Objective | Teaching Point | Method & Activities | Time | Refs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 007.01.01 Generate IDS Alerts | Generate IDS alerts involves: What are IDS tools; run IDS tools (ex: Suricata or Snort); and rule creation for IDS. | Interactive lecture Practical Exercises | 5 x 50 mins |  |
| 007.01.02 Categorize IDS Alerts | Categorize alerts involves: identify alert types; review alert metadata; and categorize alert severity. | Interactive lecture Practical Exercises | 2 x 50 mins |  |
| 007.01.03 Prepare network traffic related to alert data | Prepare network traffic relevant to alert data: obtain relevant packet captures; isolate network traffic; and extract artifacts from network traffic. | Interactive lecture Demonstration Practical Exercises | 3 x 50 mins |  |
| 007.01.04 Determine validity of alerts | Determine validity of alerts involves: identifying behaviour of network traffic; identifying true or false positive and negative alerts; identifying reoccurring false positive patterns; recommending mitigation for false positives; and logging false positives in database. | Guided discussion | 3 x 50 mins | C150 |

