## PO 009 Analyze Malicious Activity in Logs

EO 009.01 Collect Forensic Artifacts

- Performance: Collect forensic artifacts.

- Conditions:

- given:

- supervision;

- analyst workstation;

- applicable software;

- internet connection;

- applicable references; and

- digital media for forensic imaging.

- denied:

- artificial intelligence;

- assistance; and

- unapproved tools.

- environment: computer labs with access to CSTE(Z) or unclassified internet.

- Standard: IAW specified references, the student shall collect forensic artifacts by:

- collecting the evidence;

- creating a working copy of the artifact;

- preserving the original artifact; and

- documenting relevant forensic information.

- Time Required:

- EO - 17 x 50 min periods; and

- EC - 3 x 60 min period;

- EC Review - 1 x 50 min period.

- Instructional Methods:

- interactive lecture;

- guided discussions;

- demonstration; and

- practical exercises/labs.

- Training Aids:

- display connected to instructor workstation;

- whiteboard, with markers and eraser;

- PowerPoint slides containing key information related to lessons (e.g., definitions, diagrams, etc.);

- hard drives to image;

- forensics imaging software; and

- forensics imaging hardware.

- Test Details: See Annex E, Assessment Plan.

- Remarks: Nil.

- Teaching Points:

| Lesson Objective | Teaching Point | Method & Activities | Time | Refs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 009.01.01 Explain digital forensics | Explain Digital forensics involves: definitions; key principles; forensic process: collection; examination; analysis; and reporting. tools used to extract and investigate digital devices. | Interactive lecture | 2 x 50 mins | C132, C135, and C140 |
| 009.01.02 Create a working copy of an artifact | Creating a working copy of an artifact involves: create integrity verification hashes; create copies of files and comparing to integrity hashes; use forensic imaging tools to: create a hard disk image; create a triage image; and create a memory snapshot. mitigate basic forensic countermeasures; and Use hardware and software write blockers. | Interactive lecture Practical exercises/labs | 6 x 50 mins | C132, C135, and C140 |
| 009.01.03 Collect forensics triage artifacts. | Forensic information that must be collected includes: registry hives; file system artifacts; execution artifacts; and browser artifacts. Students are given an image of a device and are expected to collect forensics information to triage. | Interactive lecture Practical exercises/labs | 8 x 50 mins | C132, C135, and C140 |
| 009.01.04 Document forensics information | Forensic information that must be documented includes: artifact type; and forensic tools and firmware used to recover artifacts. | Guided discussion | 1 x 50 mins | C132, C135, and C140 |

