| 009.02.01 Windows Event Logs | Explain Windows Events: types; sources; categories; identifiers; and forwarding windows events. Explain and demonstrate Windows Event Viewer: components; and utilize event viewer for malicious activity. | Interactive lectures Practical exercises | 7 x 50 mins | C143 |
| 009.02.02 Sysmon | Explain and demonstrate Sysmon: Sysmon logs and analysis logging architectures Sysmon configuration using XML to filter and review events Sysmon and how it relates to: active directory; user groups; permissions / shares; and PowerShell. | Interactive lecture Practical exercises | 4 x 50 mins |  |
| 009.02.03 Identify different activities | Develop methods of parsing logs to identify activities and behaviour which include: PowerShell usage; user logins; network connections; process creation/modifications; and terminal usage; and etc. | Interactive Lectures Guided Discussions Practical exercises | 4 x 50 mins |  |
