| PC 001-005 | Foundational Knowledge/Skills Assessment | Written and Practical | Summative: To assess the student’s understanding and application of key foundational knowledge and skills gained in Module 1. Assessment is not an equivalent of Module 1. | Written 240 mins  Practical 240 mins | Prior to course loading of Module 2-4 | Written: The test (closed book) will consist of a series of different types of questions: multiple choice short answer fill in the blank mix and match The topics will cover key knowledge components of Module 1. Students will require a minimum of 70% to pass the test. Practical: The test (closed book; limited tools) will consist of a series of short answer questions that require students to practically demonstrate skills and understanding of Module 1. Students will require a minimum of 70% to pass the test. To be successful on the entire assessment, students must pass both parts. | Test questions and answer key. computer lab environnement. | Progress Review Process will be applied to unsuccessful students IAW TE SOP’s. |
| EC 006.01 | Comply with DND security orders and directives. | Game | Formative: To assess the student’s understanding of security policies. | 120 minutes | On completion of EO 006.01 | The test (closed book) will consist of a series of questions in a game format that assess the student’s knowledge of security policy. | Test questions and answer key. | Progress Review Process will be applied to unsuccessful students IAW TE SOP’s. |
| EC 006.02 | Identify DND network architecture. | Practical | Formative: To assess the student’s ability to identify DND network architecture. | 120 minutes (50 mins for review) | On completion of EO 006.02 | The test (open book) will consist of a series of short answer questions that require students to practically identify network architecture. Students will require a minimum of 70% to pass the test. | Test questions and answer key. computer lab environment. internet access. | Progress Review Process will be applied to unsuccessful students IAW TE SOP’s. |
| PC 006 | Analyze DND network traffic. | Written and Practical | Summative: To assess the student’s understanding of security policies and their ability to identify DND network architecture. | Written: 60 minutes Practical: 120 minutes (50 mins for review) | On completion of EOs 006.01 and 006.02 | The first part of the test (closed book) will consist of a series of multiple choice, short answer and scenario-based questions that assess the student’s ability to apply cyber security orders and directives. Students must submit their written test before moving onto the practical portion. Students will require a minimum of 70% to pass the test. The second part of the test (closed book; limited tool availability) will consist of a series of short answer questions that require students to practically identify network architecture. Students will require a minimum of 70% to pass the test. To be successful on the PC, students must pass both parts. | Test questions and answer key. computer lab environment. internet access. | Progress Review Process will be applied to unsuccessful students IAW TE SOP’s. |
| EC 007.01-03 | Analyze malicious activity in network traffic. | Practical | Formative: To assess the student’s ability, analyze malicious activity in network traffic. | 240 mins. (50 mins for review) | On completion of EO 007.01-03.03 | Students are to analyze provided network traffic and identify any malicious activities that occurred in the traffic. Criterion: events/actions: students are required to identify complete malicious events/actions in the incident (scanning, exfiltration, lateral movement, etc.); details: parts of an event/action that detail the Who, What, Where, and When of an event; critical: certain events/actions are considered critical to the incident and failing to report on all will result in test failure; and analysis: define the “So What” alongside the How and Why of actions/activities. Students must submit a written report by the end of the EC documenting all the technical items relevant to reconstructing the malicious activity. The report must be Complete (all sections) Clear Follows course report template This assessment is marked as a pass/fail. | Test questions and answer key. computer lab environment. internet access. | Progress Review Process will be applied to unsuccessful students IAW TE SOP’s. |
| PC 007 | Analyze malicious activity in network traffic. | Practical | Summative: To assess the student’s ability, analyze malicious activity in network traffic. | 240 mins. (50 mins for review) | On completion of PO 007 | Students are to analyze provided network traffic and identify any malicious activities that occurred in the traffic. Criterion: events/actions: students are required to identify complete malicious events/actions in the incident (scanning, exfiltration, lateral movement, etc.); details: parts of an event/action that detail the Who, What, Where, and When of an event; critical: certain events/actions are considered critical to the incident and failing to report on all will result in test failure; and analysis: define the “So What” alongside the How and Why of actions/activities. Students must submit a written report by the end of the PC documenting all the technical items relevant to reconstructing the malicious activity. The report must be Complete (all sections) Clear Follows course report template This assessment is marked as a pass/fail. | Test questions and answer key. computer lab environment. internet access. | Progress Review Process will be applied to unsuccessful students IAW TE SOP’s. |
