**Legend**:

Test Types – Theory or Practical (IAW CFITES Vol 7)

Assessment Purpose – Formative or Summative (IAW CFITES Vol 7); what is the student being assessed on (ie, assess their ability to)?

Test Description – May include details about the testing event’s intent, minimum standard for pass i.e. 70%, or P/F checklist, individual or group testing, etc. It should contain enough details to ensure that the intent of the test is not missed during the development phase.

# ANNEX E - TRAINING DELIVERY REFORM POTENTIAL

This Annex is used to compel SMEs to think about every training delivery possibility.  The board must consider TDR (post-secondary training and educational institutions, such as community colleges, Distance learning (DL), E-learning, etc.)  Depending on the nature of learning events, this annex can be completed at the PO level, at the EO level or at the teaching point level.1

| PO # | EO # | Teaching Point | TDR | Remarks |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 001 - 005 | N/A | ALL | 100% | Post-secondary training and education for POs 001 - 005 will delivered by an accredited Canadian institution recognized through the CAF-ACE as being aligned with CYBER OP training and education requirements. |
| 006 - 010 | N/A | Nil. | 0% | Training associated with this PO is CAF-specific and must be delivered in-house at the SECRET level. |

1 If entire EO has potential for the same type of TDR, omit listing all teaching points.

